{"id": "EUVD-2016-10921", "enisaUuid": "fddb9c25-7fa1-364a-a13a-ad56ff09dc65", "description": "EyeLock nano NXT 3.05.1193, 3.04.1108, 3.03.944, and 3.01.646 contain a path traversal vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to read arbitrary files via the 'path' parameter. Attackers can send GET requests to /scripts/logdownload.php with traversal sequences like ../../etc/passwd, which readfile() returns unvalidated, disclosing local system files. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-19.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:31:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T20:31:29", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.zeroscience.mk/advisories/ZSL-2016-5356.html", "https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/40227", "https://packetstorm.news/files/id/138274/", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/other/eyelock-nano-lfd.yaml", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/eyelock-nano-nxt-3.05.1193-path-traversal-via-logdownload-php"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r7vf-jgv9-h5jm", "CVE-2016-20104"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0864b7d7-7b0c-3239-8b50-520dc29b8d32", "product": {"name": "nano NXT", "vendor": {"name": "EyeLock"}}, "product_version": "3.04.1108"}, {"id": "08ad5da7-48da-3c5b-9120-adc2a178271f", "product": {"name": "nano NXT", "vendor": {"name": "EyeLock"}}, "product_version": "3.05.1193"}, {"id": "220cae8a-f65d-3f0a-83cc-fbb4fdb2a222", "product": {"name": "nano NXT", "vendor": {"name": "EyeLock"}}, "product_version": "3.03.944"}, {"id": "8dc2fcff-06b9-3c5e-88e6-e8062842e1b7", "product": {"name": "nano NXT", "vendor": {"name": "EyeLock"}}, "product_version": "3.01.646"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "059ca1b2-cb85-3416-a83d-207550bd7ca1", "vendor": {"name": "EyeLock"}}], "isExploited": false}